      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. i guess what i'm wondering is, if you were looking at a news report about a protest that got a bit loud or messy—say, some property was damaged or streets were blocked—would the media's choice to label it a \"riot\" vs a \"protest\" depend on the racial makeup of the crowd? like, is there a threshold where a white group's actions are still seen as \"passionate activism\" but a minority group's actions are immediately classified as \"criminality\"?",
